[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m # cargo feature flags in the Rust crate:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m grep -n "\[features\]" translation/Cargo.toml     # -> no matches
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Findings that bound this table:**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - The public API is exactly ONE entry point, `void driver(int x)`, and it is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   simultaneously the highest- *and* lowest-level entry point — there is no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   convenience wrapper layered over a lower-level API, no init/config/run
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   three-step pipeline, and no state to set up. `nm -D` confirms `driver` is the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   only exported symbol (see `SYMBOLS.md`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - There are ZERO runtime options, modes or flags: no enum parameters, no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   bitmask flags, no context/handle, no globals, no environment reads, no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `#ifdef`-selected variants. So the option axis of the cross-product is a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   single point, and the cross-product reduces to the input-shape axis alone.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - The Rust crate declares no `[features]`, so the only feature combination is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the default one (see the "Feature combinations" section below).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The remaining axes the code genuinely distinguishes are therefore the *value
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m classes of the single `int` argument*, which fall out of the two arithmetic
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m operations (`2*x`, `+300`) and of `printf("%d\n", ...)` formatting:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **arithmetic regime**: no overflow / add-only overflow / multiply overflow
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (positive) / multiply overflow (negative);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **sign of the printed result**: positive, zero, negative (`%d` emits a `-`);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **field width of the printed result**: 1..10 digits, i.e. every digit-count
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `%d` can produce, plus the widest negative (`-2147483648`, 11 chars);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **argument-register shape at the ABI boundary**: clean 32-bit argument vs a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   64-bit argument word with non-zero upper half (callee reads `%edi` only);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m - **call multiplicity / stdio state**: single call vs many calls in sequence
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   (exercises stdio buffering and that no hidden state accumulates between
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   calls), and interleaving C and Rust calls against the same `stdout`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Configuration-surface table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Each row = one meaningful combination of the axes above that the C treats
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m differently. Every row is driven through *both* `.so` exports with MANY
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    59[0m:[38;5;10m[49m randomized inputs (fixed seed `0x5EED_D1FF_C0FFEE01`, see
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    60[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `tests/differential.rs`), not one hand-picked value; the assertion is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    61[0m:[38;5;10m[49m byte-for-byte equality of everything written to `stdout`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    62[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    63[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    64[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|----------------|-------------------------------------------|-----|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    65[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C1 | `driver` | No options exist. Small positive `x` in `[1, 1000]`, no overflow, result positive, 3-4 printed digits. Randomized. | [ ] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    66[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C2 | `driver` | Small negative `x` in `[-1000, -1]`: result may be positive OR negative (`2x+300` crosses zero at `x = -150`), exercising the `-` sign path. Randomized. | [ ] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    67[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C3 | `driver` | `x = 0` — the "empty"/identity input. Prints the bare constant `300`. Deterministic single value. | [ ] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    68[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C4 | `driver` | `x` chosen so the result is exactly `0` (`x = -150`) and exactly `±1` (`x = -149`, `x = -151`) — sign-transition boundary of `%d`. Deterministic. | [ ] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    69[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C5 | `driver` | Result digit-count sweep: `x` chosen so `2x+300` has 1,2,3,...,10 digits, positive and negative, incl. `-2147483648` (widest). Deterministic set + randomized within each width band. | [ ] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    70[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C6 | `driver` | Mid-range `x` in `[1001, 1073741673]`: no overflow at all, large positive result. Randomized. | [ ] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    71[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C7 | `driver` | Add-only-overflow band `x` in `[1073741674, 1073741823]`: `2*x` fits, `+300` wraps. Randomized. | [ ] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    72[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C8 | `driver` | Multiply-overflow band, positive: `x` in `[1073741824, INT_MAX]`. Randomized. | [ ] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    73[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C9 | `driver` | Multiply-overflow band, negative: `x` in `[INT_MIN, -1073741825]`. Randomized. | [ ] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    74[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C10 | `driver` | Mid-range negative, no overflow: `x` in `[-1073741824, -1001]`. Randomized. | [ ] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    75[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C11 | `driver` | Unrestricted full-range `x` drawn uniformly from all 2^32 values (all four arithmetic regimes mixed), many iterations. Randomized. | [ ] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    76[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C12 | `driver` | Powers of two and their neighbours (`±(1<<k)`, `±(1<<k)-1`, `±(1<<k)+1` for `k = 0..31`) — bit-pattern shapes the `lea`/`add` sequence could plausibly special-case. Deterministic sweep. | [ ] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    77[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C13 | `driver` | ABI shape: same value passed through a `void(*)(i64)`-typed pointer with non-zero upper 32 bits (and as an out-of-range "enum" value). Callee must read the low half only. Randomized. | [ ] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    78[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C14 | `driver` | Call multiplicity / no residual state: a long randomized sequence of calls through the SAME `dlopen` handle, output accumulated across all calls and compared as one byte stream (stdio buffering + statelessness). Randomized. | [ ] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    79[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | C15 | `driver` | Interleaved C/Rust calls against the same process `stdout` (alternating C, Rust, C, Rust ...), verifying identical interleaving/flush behaviour rather than merely identical per-call bytes. Randomized. | [ ] |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    80[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    81[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Feature combinations
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    82[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    83[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `translation/Cargo.toml` declares no `[features]` table and no optional
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    84[0m:[38;5;10m[49m dependencies, so the complete set of feature combinations is:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    85[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    86[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | combination | command |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    87[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |-------------|---------|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    88[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | default (= empty feature set) | `cargo test` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    89[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | explicit no-default-features (identical, since there are no default features) | `cargo test --no-default-features` |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    90[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    91[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Both are executed by `run_all.sh`; there is no third configuration to cover.
